#import "lib.typ": *

= Cockpit View

Ride along with any aircraft on the radar. Open its details with *C*, then press *A*. On a six-button
controller, *Y* goes straight there for the selected aircraft. *B* takes you back to the radar.

#align(center, shot("cockpit", width: 70%, callouts: ((1, 300, 50), (2, 300, 140), (3, 14, 160), (4, 172, 180), (5, 300, 212))))
#v(1mm)
#key(1)[The view][Straight ahead over the real ground, drawn by your Genesis as the aircraft flies.
  Turns tilt the horizon.]
#key(2)[Aircraft][callsign, type, operator; *LIVE*, *NO SIGNAL* or *TERRAIN...* (loading).]
#key(3)[Instruments][Altitude (ft), speed (kt), climb (ft/min), heading, bank (*L* or *R*).]
#key(4)[From home][Bearing and distance from your home airport.]
#key(5)[Credit][Where the ground comes from (see _Credits_).]

The relay sends the ground and the aircraft's position every two seconds; your Genesis flies smoothly
in between. Getting in takes a few seconds.

#note[What you're seeing][Hills are true to scale, so flat country looks flat. Colours come from height,
not photographs; the sky follows the real time of day.]
